{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44245850",
      "title": "What are Form Actions?",
      "sourceHash": "d163c5bd6e987b68abbc5648c680be1f34419a48ffeaf247fede9d642d28ae71",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "So what's this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 8.19,
          "en": "Form Actions feature all about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.19,
          "end": 9.75,
          "en": "Well, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.75,
          "end": 14.28,
          "en": "it's available in React version 19 or higher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.28,
          "end": 17.94,
          "en": "So if you're working in a React project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.94,
          "end": 20.58,
          "en": "that uses an older version of React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.58,
          "end": 22.893,
          "en": "you can't use this feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.15,
          "end": 27.12,
          "en": "So you should check your package.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.12,
          "end": 30.393,
          "en": "to verify that you're at least using version 19.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.5,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "And if you are using such a version,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 39.12,
          "en": "you can simply use a new feature kind of built into React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.12,
          "end": 42.48,
          "en": "that helps you with handling form submissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.48,
          "end": 45.863,
          "en": "Because in the previous section you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.863,
          "end": 48.417,
          "en": "that you can, of course, handle form submissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.417,
          "end": 51.57,
          "en": "by adding this onSubmit prop to the form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.57,
          "end": 53.64,
          "en": "And then you can point at a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.64,
          "end": 57.243,
          "en": "that should be executed when that form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.47,
          "end": 62.433,
          "en": "So here we could add a new function handleSubmit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 67.2,
          "en": "and then use that as a value for onSubmit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.2,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "And in that function, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "you would get an event object automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 75.27,
          "en": "and you would have to call event.preventDefault()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.27,
          "end": 77.49,
          "en": "to prevent that browser default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.49,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "which otherwise would be to send an HTTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.33,
          "end": 83.64,
          "en": "and we don't want that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 83.64,
          "end": 85.28999999999999,
          "en": "Now, just to be very clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.28999999999999,
          "end": 88.47,
          "en": "you can absolutely still use that approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 88.47,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "There is nothing wrong with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 93.09,
          "en": "And indeed you'll see this approach being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.09,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "in many React projects out there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "no matter which version they use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 100.56,
          "en": "You can use this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.56,
          "end": 104.94,
          "en": "but if you are using React version 19 or higher,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.94,
          "end": 108.99000000000001,
          "en": "you can also set this function handleSubmit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.99000000000001,
          "end": 113.52000000000001,
          "en": "as a value for the action prop on the form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.52000000000001,
          "end": 115.203,
          "en": "and that's new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.1,
          "end": 121.1,
          "en": "Now, this action prop is not really a new prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "Form elements support the action prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 126.81,
          "en": "or the action attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.81,
          "end": 130.95,
          "en": "no matter if you are using React or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.95,
          "end": 134.01,
          "en": "Well, the prop is supported if you're using React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.01,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "because props are a React feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 139.11,
          "en": "But even in non-React projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 139.11,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "you could set a action attribute on the form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 144.153,
          "en": "That's what I mean.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.669,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "And normally when not using React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 152.28,
          "en": "this action attribute here would be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.28,
          "end": 155.97,
          "en": "to define the path or the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.97,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "to which the browser sends the form data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 161.01,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.01,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "So that would be the default behavior which we're preventing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 166.59,
          "en": "by calling event.preventDefault().",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.59,
          "end": 169.8,
          "en": "Now, in React, when adding the action prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.8,
          "end": 173.16,
          "en": "to a form element, this is not what will happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.16,
          "end": 178.16,
          "en": "Instead, React kind of overrides this attribute, this prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.22,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "and React will make sure that this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 185.34,
          "en": "which you pass as a value to action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.34,
          "end": 188.97,
          "en": "will be executed when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 188.97,
          "end": 191.22,
          "en": "So React will do that for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.22,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "and React will behind the scenes call preventDefault",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 198.87,
          "en": "for you so that that browser default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.87,
          "end": 201.6,
          "en": "is suppressed and is not happening,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.6,
          "end": 204.123,
          "en": "and that instead this function is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.17000000000002,
          "end": 207.42000000000002,
          "en": "Now, this function then, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 207.42000000000002,
          "end": 211.05,
          "en": "will no longer get an event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.05,
          "end": 214.32,
          "en": "Instead, that function when used as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.32,
          "end": 218.583,
          "en": "for the action prop will get a formData object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.9,
          "end": 222.48,
          "en": "The same kind of formData object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.48,
          "end": 225.87,
          "en": "you could create manually based on a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.87,
          "end": 228.87,
          "en": "as we did it in the previous section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.87,
          "end": 231.03,
          "en": "There I showed you that you can construct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.03,
          "end": 234.15,
          "en": "a formData object based on the event target,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.15,
          "end": 236.79,
          "en": "which was the submitted form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 239.22,
          "en": "Now, when using this form actions feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 239.22,
          "end": 242.22,
          "en": "this formData object is created automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 242.22,
          "end": 244.71,
          "en": "for you by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.71,
          "end": 248.01,
          "en": "And this formData object then will contain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 248.01,
          "end": 249.51,
          "en": "all the submitted data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.51,
          "end": 252.93,
          "en": "so all the submitted input values in that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.93,
          "end": 256.98,
          "en": "For that it's just important that you add the name prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.98,
          "end": 258.75,
          "en": "to all your input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 258.75,
          "end": 261.93,
          "en": "because that name prop sets the key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.93,
          "end": 266.82,
          "en": "which is then used in the formData to extract the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 266.82,
          "end": 268.623,
          "en": "for the different input fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.52,
          "end": 272.67,
          "en": "So you must add the name prop to your inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.67,
          "end": 274.44,
          "en": "for that inputs value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 274.44,
          "end": 277.383,
          "en": "to be included in that formData object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 278.4,
          "end": 281.523,
          "en": "But we're already doing that here in this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 286.53,
          "en": "And then here in handleSubmit we can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.53,
          "end": 291.53,
          "en": "get the entered email by accessing formData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.65999999999997,
          "end": 293.15999999999997,
          "en": "and calling the get method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.15999999999997,
          "end": 295.95,
          "en": "that's built into this formData object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 295.95,
          "end": 300.54,
          "en": "And then we extract the value for the key email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.54,
          "end": 302.16,
          "en": "And I'm using the key email here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.16,
          "end": 304.44,
          "en": "because I used email as a name down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 304.44,
          "end": 306.483,
          "en": "So that's how this is related.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 307.98,
          "end": 309.87,
          "en": "So that then gives me the entered email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 309.87,
          "end": 312.63,
          "en": "And, of course, we could extract all the data now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 312.63,
          "end": 314.91,
          "en": "but here I'll just start with the email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.91,
          "end": 317.34,
          "en": "and then we can console.log(enteredEmail)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 317.34,
          "end": 320.343,
          "en": "just so that we see something on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 321.72,
          "end": 325.03,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if we save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 325.92,
          "end": 328.27,
          "en": "and we go back and open the developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.21,
          "end": 332.13,
          "en": "and clear the console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.13,
          "end": 336.6,
          "en": "if I enter some email address here and I click Sign Up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 336.6,
          "end": 338.55,
          "en": "I can see that email here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.55,
          "end": 342.213,
          "en": "So that's Reacts form actions feature in action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 343.40999999999997,
          "end": 347.34000000000003,
          "en": "You also might notice that the form was reset,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.34000000000003,
          "end": 350.76,
          "en": "the email field was cleared because that's also something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 350.76,
          "end": 353.4,
          "en": "React does automatically for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 353.4,
          "end": 357.21,
          "en": "And I'll soon show you how you can work around that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 357.21,
          "end": 360.66,
          "en": "how you can make sure that user values are being saved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 360.66,
          "end": 362.97,
          "en": "and kept if you want that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.97,
          "end": 364.92,
          "en": "But for the moment it's enough to see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 364.92,
          "end": 367.473,
          "en": "that this form actions feature works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 368.34,
          "end": 370.92,
          "en": "Now, there's just one more thing I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 370.92,
          "end": 374.953,
          "en": "I'll rename this function to signUpAction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.56,
          "end": 378.45,
          "en": "and also use that new name here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.45,
          "end": 381.9,
          "en": "because whilst the old name, of course, also worked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.9,
          "end": 385.95,
          "en": "I no longer want to use this handleSubmit name here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.95,
          "end": 389.25,
          "en": "because we're not really handling the submit event anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 389.25,
          "end": 393.33,
          "en": "Instead, we create a function that serves as a form action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.33,
          "end": 395.73,
          "en": "And that's why I'm using this naming pattern.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 395.73,
          "end": 397.44,
          "en": "But that's, of course, optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 397.44,
          "end": 399.543,
          "en": "and just personal preference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 400.62,
          "end": 404.07,
          "en": "But with that, we created our first form action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 404.07,
          "end": 406.983,
          "en": "and we let React handle the form submission now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}